# Commercial S3.2 baseline-index invocation diagnosis

Date: 2026-08-29
Decision: SAFE_ABORT_BEFORE_REPOSITORY_DELTA

The exact-replay server delta stopped before any Git fetch or checkout because
`sha256sum --check` was invoked with an absolute index path while the current
directory was not the baseline directory. The index intentionally contains
relative member names, so six members were reported as unreadable.

Read-only post-abort verification proved that the application and Control
repositories remained at their previous SHA/tree pairs, both worktrees stayed
clean, the service remained `inactive/dead`, `NRestarts=0`, and no main process
existed. The newly allocated evidence directory contained no files.

The bounded correction is invocation-only: execute each check from
`/opt/tu1nz_repos/backups/commercial-s3-1-fix/20260829T13-56-54Z`, matching the
already versioned probe controller. No hash, index, baseline member, repository,
contract, unit or database state is changed. A failed corrected check remains
RED and aborts before repository mutation.
